  "note": "cs-sandbox 44eb5b5: the opencode turn driver now runs a turn against one server. It used to boot a transient `opencode serve` to mint a session id and kill it before launching the TUI on the same port, and a turn that died in that window left it holding the port, where it answered every later health check while the TUI it shadowed rendered nothing (cs-sandbox SBX-023). A server found there with no tmux session behind it is now reclaimed by name. The driver also falls back to $HOME, out loud, when the working directory it is handed does not exist. Validated with make test-smoke on this binary, not make test-integration: all five scenarios PASS on real machines. Real-provider traffic was not re-run."
